    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the others are support classes). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (the controller behind `POST /api/owners`).\n\n**What changed** in `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Read the header without changing the generated API signature.** `addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` is an `@Override` of the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi`, so I couldn't add a `@RequestHeader` parameter. Instead I inject a Spring request-scoped `HttpServletRequest` via the constructor and read `Idempotency-Key` from it.\n\n2. **Idempotency store.** A static `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer>` (`IDEMPOTENT_CREATES`) remembers which owner id each seen key produced.\n\n3. **Create flow.** `addOwner` now:\n   - If a non-blank `Idempotency-Key` is present and already mapped to an owner that still exists, it returns that owner rendered the same way `getOwner` does (household member count + bulk-signup warning) with **200 OK** \u2014 no duplicate created.\n   - Otherwise it runs the normal create pipeline (returning **201 Created** with the `Location` header as before), and records `key \u2192 new owner id` when a key was supplied.\n\nA blank/absent key behaves exactly as before. The lookup tolerates a key pointing at an owner that no longer exists (e.g. rolled back) by falling through to a normal create.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreIdempotentRepeat` \u2014 which posts the same owner twice with one key and asserts the second call returns 200 with the same id \u2014 passes, as does the full build.",
