    "probe_text": "I have the full picture. The creation flow runs entirely inside `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2192 `createOwner`, with derived fields (region, membershipLevel/Number) computed lazily by getters on the `Owner` model. Here is the ordered sequence.\n\n## Ordered flow for `POST /api/owners` (`addOwner`)\n\n**Authorization (before the method body)**\n1. **`@PreAuthorize hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)`** \u2014 caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n\n**Idempotency short-circuit** (`addOwner`, lines 139\u2013152)\n2. **Read `Idempotency-Key` header** (`idempotencyKey()`), trimmed; blank/absent \u2192 treated as none.\n3. **Idempotent replay** (`replayIdempotentCreate`): if that key already created an owner *and* that owner still exists, stamp its `householdMemberCount`, map it, set `bulkSignupWarning`, and **return 200 OK with the original owner** \u2014 no new owner is created. Otherwise fall through.\n\n**Registration date** (`effectiveRegistrationDate`, lines 213 / 424\u2013431)\n4. **Validation:** a supplied `registrationDate` later than today \u2192 400 `InvalidFieldsException(\"registrationDate\")`.\n5. **Side-effect:** compute the effective date = supplied-or-`now`, then **roll forward to the next business day** (skipping Sat/Sun and the fixed 2026 public-holiday set).\n\n**Intake pipeline** (`prepareNewOwner`, lines 357\u2013366) \u2014 in this exact order:\n6. **Side-effect \u2014 normalize address** (`applyAddress`): if `addressLine1` is non-blank, normalize the structured lines and recompose the flat `address`; otherwise normalize the flat `address`. Normalization = trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`. (Runs first so a blank-after-normalization address is caught next.)\n7. **Validation \u2014 required fields** (`validateRequiredFields`): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank \u2192 else 400 `RequiredFieldsMissingException` listing all offenders.\n8. **Side-effect + validation \u2014 normalize telephone** (`normalizeTelephone`): strip spaces/dashes/brackets, coerce to E.164 (assume `+61`, drop leading `0`); must match `+` and 8\u201315 digits, and (for recognized country codes) the correct national-number length \u2192 else 400 `InvalidFieldsException(\"telephone\")`.\n9. **Side-effect + validation \u2014 normalize email** (`normalizeEmail`): `null` allowed; otherwise must match the email pattern and not be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), stored trimmed + lower-cased \u2192 else 400 `InvalidFieldsException(\"email\")`.\n10. **Validation \u2014 postcode** (`validatePostcode`): `null` allowed; otherwise must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region, within that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else 400 `InvalidFieldsException(\"postcode\")`.\n11. **Validation \u2014 household duplicate** (`rejectDuplicateIdentity`): unless `sharesHousehold` is true, if any non-deleted owner already carries the `householdId` derived from `(lastName, postcode)` \u2192 409 `DuplicateIdentityException`. (Owners with no postcode are never household duplicates.)\n12. **Validation \u2014 city capacity** (`rejectCityAtCapacity`): if the city (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 409 `CityCapacityExceededException`.\n13. **Validation \u2014 daily limit** (`rejectDailyLimitExceeded`): if \u2265 100 existing owners already carry that effective `registrationDate` \u2192 429 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n\n**Build, derive, persist** (`createOwner`, lines 215\u2013226)\n14. **Side-effect \u2014 map** DTO \u2192 `Owner` (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, id/pets ignored).\n15. **Side-effect \u2014 set `registrationDate`** to the effective business-day date.\n16. **Side-effect \u2014 set `customerCode`** (`customerCodeFor`): `\"<REGION>-<HASH8>\"` (region or `UNKNOWN`, HASH8 = first 8 hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`), then **de-duplicated** against existing codes by appending `-<n>` (n \u2265 2).\n17. **Side-effect \u2014 set `namesakeCount`**: count of pre-existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n18. **Side-effect \u2014 assign `householdId`** (`assignHousehold`): SHA-256-derived id from `(lastName, postcode)`, or `null` when no postcode.\n19. **Side-effect \u2014 flag possible (soft) duplicate** (`applyPossibleDuplicate`): default false; skipped when `sharesHousehold`; otherwise set `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when a non-deleted owner shares last name + postcode but has a different telephone.\n20. **Side-effect \u2014 persist** the owner (`clinicService.saveOwner`), assigning its generated id.\n21. **Side-effect \u2014 set `householdMemberCount`** (`countHouseholdMembers`), now counting the just-saved owner.\n22. **Side-effect \u2014 audit log**: `AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: ...\")` with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and the lazily-derived membershipLevel/membershipNumber.\n\n**Record idempotency + respond** (`addOwner` 148\u2013151, `createdOwnerResponse`)\n23. **Side-effect \u2014 record idempotency**: if a key was supplied, store `key \u2192 owner.id` in the shared `IDEMPOTENT_CREATES` map.\n24. **Side-effect \u2014 build 201 response** (`createdOwnerResponse`): map to `OwnerDto`, set `bulkSignupWarning` (true when > 80 owners share the registration date), attach `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\nA couple of notes: the derived `region`, `membershipLevel`, and `membershipNumber` aren't stored during creation \u2014 they're computed on read by getters on the `Owner`/mapper, so they only appear via the audit log and the response DTO. Also worth flagging that the idempotency store and all the count/capacity/duplicate checks read the full owner list without a surrounding transaction or lock, so under concurrency the caps and duplicate checks are best-effort rather than strictly serialized \u2014 but you asked me only to read and report, so I've changed nothing."
